+# Sprint 1 demo runbook
+
+This runbook describes the reproducible engineering demonstration for issues #12, #21, #22, #23, #24, #37, #39, #43 and #44. It does not represent a submitted course video or approval. The demo uses synthetic users, coordinates and credits.
+
+## Start and verify
+
+From a clean checkout, confirm Docker Compose, Python 3, Node.js and an available local port, then run:
+
+```sh
+cd prototype
+sh reproduction/verify-package.sh
+sh reproduction/start-local.sh
+python3 reproduction/smoke-booking.py
+```
+
+Open `http://127.0.0.1:18180/mobility/?demo=campus-route` in separate driver and rider browser profiles. Stop the disposable stack with `sh reproduction/stop-local.sh` after the capture. Do not use production credentials, real student data or a production database.
+
+The portable demo uses deterministic synthetic routing. It does not establish live Maps/OSRM behavior, college identity verification, GPS tracking, payment settlement or production readiness. A routing-provider failure must leave readable pickup and fare summaries visible; it is not evidence of real road navigation.
+
+## One-minute script
+
+| Time | Action and spoken evidence |
+|---|---|
+| 0–10 s | State that this is a synthetic CampusPool demo. Show the actual vehicle summary and verification label. Demo eligibility is not vehicle approval: if no current approved onboarding exists, show the unverified label and explain that approval remains pending. Keep licence data private. |
+| 10–22 s | Publish one future ride with origin, destination, vehicle and the displayed one-passenger Sprint 1 limit. Use the focused tests as separate evidence for rejected past times and invalid seat counts. |
+| 22–34 s | As the rider, search the same date and compatible direction. Show host, the actual available vehicle metadata, free seats and pickup/fare summary. Explain that an empty result or routing failure remains readable. |
+| 34–46 s | Request one seat, show the pending state, accept as the driver, and show the rider's confirmed state. The rider and driver must be distinct synthetic accounts. |
+| 46–60 s | Cancel the booking as the authorized participant. Show the cancelled history, one refund/credit effect and restored capacity. Repeat the cancel action only to demonstrate that it is idempotent. |
+
+Keep the capture continuous. A script, screenshot or test log is evidence of preparation; it is not a substitute for the actual recorded UI video.
+
+## Evidence checklist
+
+- [ ] Fresh-clone package verification completed with its exit status recorded.
+- [ ] Focused backend and frontend tests recorded with command, revision and assertion counts.
+- [ ] Driver/rider accounts are synthetic and visibly distinct.
+- [ ] Current approved vehicle metadata is visible before confirmation when an approved onboarding exists; any unverified demo fallback is described honestly.
+- [ ] Invalid future time, capacity and malformed search input show useful errors.
+- [ ] Search excludes full, cancelled, unpublished, incompatible and out-of-window rides.
+- [ ] Self-booking, unauthorized acceptance, duplicate request and competing last-seat cases have automated evidence.
+- [ ] Cancellation retains history, restores capacity and does not duplicate a refund.
+- [ ] Any routing-provider failure and known limitation is stated during the demo.
+- [ ] The real one-minute recording is reviewed before uploading through a reviewed media PR linked to #44.
+
+## Academic reconciliation
+
+The owner reports that the documents may not have been created. Gmail/Drive searches found faculty templates and the team plan but no submitted/approved versions. New SRS, SAD, Test Plan and RTM drafts are included; obtain instructor acceptance of the appropriate versions. Traceability remains provisional; new proposed IDs are not historical submitted IDs. The engineering package can be ready while the academic submission remains pending. The Sprint 2 waitlist/rematching behavior is outside the Sprint 1 cancellation demonstration.
+
+For the final handoff, attach the exact baseline SHA, issue/PR links, focused test output, migration result and recording URL. Preserve contributor attribution and third-party notices. Never claim a recording, review, upload or faculty approval that has not actually occurred.
