+# Software Requirements Specification (SRS) — CampusPool
+
+**Project:** CampusPool student carpooling and bikepooling
+**Version:** 0.1 (proposed draft)
+**Date:** 26 October 2026
+**Status:** DRAFT — not submitted, approved, or signed
+**Authors:** To be completed by the student team; this package is AI-assisted proposed documentation.
+
+## Revision history
+
+| Version | Date | Author | Change | Approval |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0.1 | 2026-10-26 | Proposed package | Initial reconstruction from current prototype and course templates | None |
+
+## Approvals
+
+No approval has been recorded. Course coordinator, team and instructor fields must be completed by the students if this draft is adopted.
+
+## 1. Introduction
+
+### 1.1 Purpose
+
+This draft specifies a campus commute application in which a verified or locally synthetic driver publishes a future car/bike ride and a rider searches, requests, confirms and cancels a seat.
+
+### 1.2 Scope
+
+The current engineering baseline covers a Laravel/MySQL API, browser commute UI, deterministic synthetic routing, vehicle and ride metadata, matching, booking lifecycle, cancellation and demo wallet records. College identity, production routing, live GPS, real payments, Next.js and NoSQL/vector storage are outside this Sprint 1 package.
+
+### 1.3 Audience
+
+Students, instructors, developers, testers, reviewers and future maintainers.
+
+### 1.4 Definitions
+
+Driver/host: ride publisher. Rider/passenger: seat requester. Quote: signed, time-bound search result. Booking: rider request and lifecycle state. Synthetic demo: isolated fixture mode with nonredeemable credits. RTM: requirements traceability matrix. STP: software test plan.
+
+## 2. Overall description
+
+### 2.1 Product perspective
+
+The browser client calls a Laravel API. MySQL is authoritative for users, vehicles, trips, bookings, lifecycle states and demo wallet entries. A routing adapter supplies synthetic route terms in the portable test environment.
+
+### 2.2 Major product functions
+
+The proposed functional requirements are:
+
+| ID | Requirement | Priority |
+|---|---|---|
+| CP-F-001 | The system shall create distinct driver and rider sessions in synthetic evaluation mode. | High |
+| CP-F-002 | The system shall save a user commute profile with role, vehicle preference, home, campus, schedule and weekdays. | High |
+| CP-F-003 | The system shall show driver approval state without allowing a user to self-approve. | High |
+| CP-F-004 | The system shall record vehicle type, model/registration summary and legal passenger-seat capacity. | High |
+| CP-F-005 | The system shall prevent a rider from publishing an offer when the role or approval policy is not eligible. | High |
+| CP-F-006 | The system shall publish a future car or bike offer with origin, destination, departure window and seat limit. | High |
+| CP-F-007 | The system shall reject past departures and capacities above the configured vehicle limit. | High |
+| CP-F-008 | The system shall make duplicate publish requests idempotent. | Medium |
+| CP-F-009 | The system shall search future offers by date, direction, time window, vehicle and pickup choice. | High |
+| CP-F-010 | The system shall exclude cancelled, unpublished, full, incompatible and out-of-window offers. | High |
+| CP-F-011 | The system shall return readable pickup, drop-off and fare summaries when routing data is unavailable. | High |
+| CP-F-012 | The system shall issue a quote token bound to the searched ride and request context. | High |
+| CP-F-013 | The system shall reject self-booking and requests from unauthorized actors. | High |
+| CP-F-014 | The system shall prevent duplicate pending or confirmed requests for the same rider and ride. | High |
+| CP-F-015 | The system shall permit an eligible driver to accept or reject a pending request. | High |
+| CP-F-016 | The system shall reserve a seat atomically and prevent simultaneous acceptances from overselling capacity. | High |
+| CP-F-017 | The system shall expose pending, confirmed and cancelled booking history to the appropriate participant. | High |
+| CP-F-018 | The system shall permit an authorized participant to cancel a booking and restore capacity exactly once. | High |
+| CP-F-019 | The system shall make repeated cancellation safe and prevent duplicate refund effects. | High |
+| CP-F-020 | The system shall retain database relationships, state constraints and audit-relevant wallet entries after lifecycle changes. | High |
+
+### 2.3 User roles and characteristics
+
+The product roles are driver/host and rider/passenger. An operator or instructor may inspect synthetic evidence. Production identity and role approval are not established by this draft.
+
+### 2.4 Operating environment
+
+Portable verification uses Docker Compose, PHP/Laravel, MySQL 8, Python 3 and Node.js on a local or GitHub Actions Linux runner. The UI is served on `127.0.0.1:18180`.
+
+### 2.5 Constraints and assumptions
+
+The current package uses synthetic routing and data. It does not claim real road navigation, payment settlement, identity verification, production availability or an approved course submission.
+
+## 3. External interface requirements
+
+### 3.1 User interfaces
+
+The browser UI provides onboarding, vehicle/ride fields, search, request, acceptance and cancellation status. The driver and rider should be shown in separate browser profiles during demonstration.
+
+### 3.2 Software interfaces
+
+Representative API resources are `/api/mobility/commute/profile`, `/offers`, `/rides`, `/rides/{trip}/request`, `/bookings`, `/bookings/{booking}/accept|reject|cancel`, `/wallet` and `/wallet/top-up`.
+
+### 3.3 Communications
+
+JSON over HTTP is used in the local demo. Production TLS, authentication provider and provider credentials require a separate design and review.
+
+## 4. System features and requirements
+
+The numbered requirements in section 2.2 are the proposed feature baseline. Exact acceptance evidence is provisional until the submitted SRS and faculty-approved Test Plan are located.
+
+## 5. Non-functional requirements
+
+| ID | Requirement | Measurement/status |
+|---|---|---|
+| CP-NF-001 | All state-changing API operations shall validate input and return a stable error shape. | Focused tests; proposed |
+| CP-NF-002 | Booking acceptance and cancellation shall use a transaction and row locks appropriate to MySQL. | Integration/concurrency tests; proposed |
+| CP-NF-003 | Sensitive identity, licence and bearer-token values shall not be written to demo output or application logs. | Review and redaction checks; proposed |
+| CP-NF-004 | A fresh checkout shall be able to verify package integrity and initialize an isolated database without developer state. | `verify-package.sh`; proposed |
+| CP-NF-005 | The commute UI shall remain usable with empty results and routing-provider failure. | Frontend harness/manual demonstration; proposed |
+| CP-NF-006 | The application shall preserve cancelled history and idempotent financial effects. | Lifecycle tests; proposed |
+
+## 6. Security objectives and requirements
+
+Objectives: (SO-1) prevent unauthorized role, booking and cancellation actions; (SO-2) minimize disclosure of identity, licence, token and financial data.
+
+| ID | Security requirement |
+|---|---|
+| CP-SEC-001 | The API shall authorize driver-only publication and acceptance actions against the authenticated actor. |
+| CP-SEC-002 | The API shall reject self-booking and unauthorized cancellation. |
+| CP-SEC-003 | Quote tokens shall be bound to the ride and request context and stale/changed quotes shall be rejected. |
+| CP-SEC-004 | Bearer tokens, licence data and private identity fields shall not appear in CI output, screenshots or demo logs. |
+| CP-SEC-005 | Synthetic demo credits shall be clearly nonredeemable and isolated from production payment systems. |
+
+## 7. Quality attributes and acceptance tests
+
+Acceptance is proposed in [RTM_DRAFT.md](RTM_DRAFT.md) and [TEST_PLAN_DRAFT.md](TEST_PLAN_DRAFT.md). No test ID in those documents is an approved faculty identifier.
+
+## 8. UML use-case diagram
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  Driver((Driver)) --> Publish[Publish ride]
+  Driver --> Accept[Accept or reject request]
+  Rider((Rider)) --> Search[Search rides]
+  Rider --> Request[Request seat]
