+# Software Test Plan (STP) — CampusPool
+
+**Project:** CampusPool Sprint 1
+**Version:** 0.1 (proposed draft)
+**Date:** 26 October 2026
+**Status:** DRAFT — not submitted, approved, or signed
+**References:** [SRS_DRAFT.md](SRS_DRAFT.md), [SAD_DRAFT.md](SAD_DRAFT.md), [RTM_DRAFT.md](RTM_DRAFT.md)
+
+## 1. Introduction
+
+**Purpose:** Define the proposed verification strategy for the CampusPool commute prototype. This document is reconstructed from the faculty STP template and current source evidence; it is not the submitted Test Plan.
+
+**Scope:** Registration/profile bridge, vehicle and ride publication, search/matching, request/accept/reject, capacity, cancellation/history, synthetic wallet effects, package integrity, migrations and browser harnesses.
+
+**References:** Proposed SRS/SAD above, official baseline `0478ae0ba2549f8fba3bd44b590e91e067a46e0d`, current issue acceptance criteria, faculty templates and DBMS requirements.
+
+**Definitions:** Driver, rider, quote token, booking, lifecycle state, synthetic demo, RTM, UAT.
+
+## 2. Test Items
+
+- Commute profile and driver/vehicle bridge
+- Ride publication and validation
+- Search/matching and quote freshness
+- Booking request, acceptance, rejection and authorization
+- Seat contention and cancellation/refund lifecycle
+- MySQL migrations, constraints and isolated database setup
+- Browser commute, map and place-search harnesses
+- CI package/source integrity and synthetic HTTP smoke journey
+
+## 3. Features to be Tested
+
+Features map to proposed SRS IDs: `CP-F-002..020`, `CP-NF-001..006` and `CP-SEC-001..005`. Concrete current test files include:
+
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/tests/MobilityCommuteProductTest.php`
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/tests/MobilitySegmentBookingTest.php`
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/tests/MobilityLifecycleTest.php`
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/tests/MobilityFinancialInvariantsTest.php`
+- `prototype/tests/frontend/test-commute-ui.mjs`
+- `prototype/tests/frontend/test-commute-map.mjs`
+- `prototype/tests/frontend/test-place-search.mjs`
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/web/driver-onboarding-ui.test.mjs`
+- `prototype/campuspool-extension/web/tracking-state.test.mjs`
+- `prototype/reproduction/smoke-booking.py`
+- `prototype/reproduction/verify-package.sh`
+
+The final integrated package must add each sibling issue worker's focused test file to this inventory after integration. Names and results must be updated from the actual checkout rather than invented here.
+
+## 4. Features Not to be Tested
+
+Production college identity provider, live road-routing/Maps/OSRM behavior, real GPS, payment settlement/payouts, native mobile clients, production uptime, Next.js client, NoSQL/vector retrieval and Sprint 2 waitlist/rematching are outside this Sprint 1 package. They require separate implementation and evidence.
+
+## 5. Test Approach / Strategy
+
+Levels are unit/service tests, integration tests against disposable MySQL, browser harness checks, package/static validation, fresh-clone verification, synthetic HTTP smoke flow and manual UAT capture. Positive, negative, boundary, authorization, idempotency and concurrency cases are required where the behavior applies.
+
+**Entry criteria:** pinned baseline, isolated checkout, disposable database, dependencies available, synthetic fixtures and test commands documented.
+
+**Exit criteria:** planned in-scope tests executed, no unresolved critical failure, package integrity passes, limitations recorded and actual evidence attached. A green synthetic run does not prove production provider behavior.
+
+### 5.1 Security Validation
+
+Validate self-booking rejection, driver-only publication/acceptance, unauthorized cancellation, duplicate requests, stale quote rejection, input validation and absence of bearer tokens/licence data in output. Do not use real credentials or student data. Production TLS, penetration testing and identity-provider review remain pending.
+
+## 6. Test Environment
+
+Docker Compose with MySQL 8, PHP/Laravel, Node.js and Python on a fresh checkout or GitHub Actions Linux runner. The local demo uses `127.0.0.1:18180`, a disposable database and synthetic route fixtures. Commands are documented in `prototype/reproduction/verify-package.sh`, `prototype/reproduction/start-local.sh` and `prototype/reproduction/smoke-booking.py`.
+
+## 7. Test Schedule
+
+The faculty handout specifies Sprint 1 as 19–23 October 2026 and Sprint 2 as 26–30 October 2026. This package is prepared on 26 October as proposed evidence; it does not assert that the original submission deadlines, video upload or approvals were met.
+
+## 8. Test Deliverables
+
+- Proposed SRS, SAD, STP and RTM drafts
+- Focused unit/integration/frontend test files
+- Package manifest and source map
+- CI logs and safe smoke output
+- Manual one-minute recording and review checklist (recording itself pending)
+- Defect notes and deviation/reconciliation report
+
+## 9. Roles and Responsibilities
+
+Roles follow the live issue assignments provisionally: Arjun (#23, #39, #44), Zayaan (#12, #21), Nikhil (#22, #43) and Nithesh (#24, #37). This table is not proof of instructor-approved two-person DBMS membership or authorship. Each student must review, understand and submit their own contribution.
+
+## 10. Risks and Mitigation
+
+| Risk | Mitigation |
+|---|---|
+| Synthetic routing hides provider failures | Keep provider behavior marked unverified; test readable fallback states. |
+| Shared service/migration conflicts | Apply issue patches in dependency order and rerun integrated tests. |
+| Missing submitted documents | Use proposed IDs only and request the actual documents. |
+| CI resource or Docker failure | Preserve logs, isolate disposable services and report blocked checks. |
+| Sensitive data in evidence | Use synthetic fixtures and redact tokens and identity/licence values. |
+
+## 11. Assumptions & Dependencies
+
+The current run assumes Docker Compose, PHP, Node.js and Python availability, a disposable MySQL service, stable fixture routing and approved access to the source baseline. It depends on issue #37 schema work for transaction evidence and issue #39 CI for repeatability.
+
+## 12. Suspension & Resumption Criteria
+
+Suspend testing if the disposable environment is unavailable, migrations fail, package integrity mismatches, or a critical authorization/data-loss defect blocks meaningful cases. Resume after the isolated environment is repaired, the failure is diagnosed and the affected tests are rerun. Never weaken assertions to obtain a pass.
+
+## 13. Test Case Management & Traceability
+
+The proposed IDs in [RTM_DRAFT.md](RTM_DRAFT.md) map requirements to actual source test files and commands. IDs prefixed `NCP-` are new proposed IDs for this package; they are not approved faculty test-case identifiers. Replace them only after locating the submitted Test Plan.
+
+## 14. Test Metrics & Reporting
+
+Record executed/passed/failed/skipped counts, assertions, migration status, package revision, environment and limitations. The previous local evidence recorded 10 backend tests/208 assertions and 25 frontend checks at prototype revision `faccb66`; that historical result is not a claim about every proposed patch or the missing academic submission.
+
+## 15. Approvals
+
+No QA lead, developer lead, product owner, course coordinator or instructor approval is recorded in this draft.
